</section>

<section>
  <h2>Collaborators</h2>
	<p><span title="Near-Earth Object Surveillance Satellite">NEOSSat</span> is  jointly funded by the <abbr title="Canadian Space Agency">CSA</abbr> and <a href="http://www.drdc-rddc.gc.ca/"><abbr title="Defence Research and Development Canada">DRDC</abbr></a>.  The satellite was built by <a href="http://www.mscinc.ca/" rel="external">Microsat Systems  Canada&nbsp;<span title="Incorporated">Inc.</span></a>, with support from  Spectral Applied Research and COM DEV International&nbsp;<abbr title="Limited">Ltd.</abbr> (formerly Routes AstroEngineering). The  <abbr title="Canadian Space Agency">CSA</abbr>  leads <span title="Near-Earth Object Surveillance Satellite">NEOSSat</span>'s space astronomy mission, and <abbr title="Defence Research and Development Canada">DRDC</abbr> is responsible for the <abbr title="High Earth Orbit Space Surveillance">HEOSS</abbr> space  surveillance mission.</p>
</section>

